          "title": "You'll want to know: noyer",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "noyer — \"to drown (as se noyer); to flood\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il s'est presque noyé dans le lac. He nearly drowned in the lake."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Reflexive for a person who drowns: il s'est noyé. Without se, to drown someone or to flood: noyer le moteur. The noun le noyer is a walnut tree."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "noyer is inherited from Latin necāre \"to kill\" (EtymDB), which in Late Latin narrowed to killing by water (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
